/-!
# KFY 18: polynomial shapes of nlogn's resampling cost bounds

Every cost function of the per-axis programs (`roundCost`, `bandCost`, `resCost`, `gresCost`,
`stCost`, `jCost`, `tabCost`, …) is bounded by a product of a few linear factors:

* the slice costs are `O(NR · (n + len + NR) · (Φ + mm + B))` (`NR` rounds over `n` outputs),
* the table builders are `O(NI · NK · (Cw + log))`.

The per-axis bounds **`sapAx_le`** and **`bapAx_le`** split the cost of one axis into the main
term (`m` slices, linear in `m · t`) and a table term (polynomial in `t` and the bit sizes).

`polyle` proves `P ≤ Q` for polynomials over `ℕ` whose difference has nonnegative coefficients.
-/

